Title: Gaze seats emit no reviewer attribution lines; writer lines cannot be appended after reviewer lines
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-10-27T18:32Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context
Raid 2026-10-27: no PR's attribution block validated strictly — seats wrote no `reviewer:` lines, and
attribution_record.py --append rejects a `writer:` line appended after reviewer lines ("fact order requires kind, pr,
writer before reviewers"), so the orchestrator's writer lines failed on most PRs. The writer line format also needed
trial and error (provider-qualified model, route, independence).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every gaze seat that runs leaves one `reviewer:` line in the PR's attribution block (or the notes answer on the no-forge path).
- [ ] Appending a writer line to a block that already has reviewer lines places it correctly instead of failing.
- [ ] The required writer and reviewer fields are documented in one place the raid and hunt cite.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

Related: [[1243]].

## Imagine (raid 2026-10-27b)
- Premise holds. `identity()` (attribution_record.py:~45) and `parse_record` (:93) are unchanged since the raid; `append_line` (:185) appends blindly before the closing fence, so a writer line after reviewers lands out of order and only the strict parse (`--pr-body`, `extract_record`) rejects it. gaze_close.py (:243) appends only what the attribution file holds; a `--seats-pr` path (roar 1155) already derives reviewer lines from the `seat:` lines of the posted result, but nothing in gaze runs it, and the raid's coder-run gazes left the file empty. No commit since Created touches these surfaces.
- Simplest path: (a) `append_line` inserts a `writer:` line before the first `reviewer:` line of the block (after the last existing `writer:` line if any); (b) gaze_close, after posting its comment, runs the existing `attribution_record.py --seats-pr <pr>` when the attribution file was empty or lacks a seat named in the comment; (c) one doc section. No new module, no new format.
- Antipattern scan: YAGNI hit if a new "attribution builder" is proposed: `--seats-pr` already skips seats present in the body, reuse it. Do not re-sort the whole block (premature); only the writer insertion point. Doc: add `## Line formats` to skills/merge/references/claims.md (it already owns "Attribution block warning"); raid and hunt cite it, no copy of the field list.
- Risk class: concrete fix, 3 sites + doc. Coder: sonnet.

## Plan
1. scripts/attribution_record.py `append_line`: when LINE starts with `writer:` and the block holds a `reviewer:` line, insert before the first one (keep multi-line LINE intact); otherwise current behaviour.
2. scripts/gaze_close.py (main, after the attribution append / comment post): non-local path, call `attribution_record.py --seats-pr <pr> --project <name>`, report `attribution: seats appended|FAILED ...` like the existing line; no forge path stays "carried in the answer entry" (answer already carries seat lines; confirm in record_answer, else add the `seat:` text there).
3. skills/merge/references/claims.md: `## Line formats`: writer fields (step, runtime, model=provider/id, effort, route, independence), reviewer fields (step, seat, ..., status), `not-stated`, masked variant, one worked line each; point to `--pr-body` as the check.
4. skills/raid/SKILL.md (Attribution lines, :250-259) and skills/hunt/SKILL.md (where writer lines are named; grep `writer:`): replace restated formats with the cite; note writer lines may be appended at any time.
5. skills/gaze/SKILL.md (:170-175): say gaze_close derives missing reviewer lines from the result's `seat:` lines.
- First test (tests/test_attribution_record.py, `test_append_writer_after_reviewers_lands_before_them`): build body with PLAN, REVIEW, GATE, then `run_append(body, EXECUTE)`; assert `parse_pr_body` succeeds, `[w.step] == [plan, execute]` and the writer line index < first reviewer index. A wrong impl that appends at the end fails parse_record on order; one that sorts everything would also pass, so add an assert the reviewer lines keep their relative order. Second: tests/test_gaze_close.py, `test_empty_attribution_file_runs_seats_pr` with a stub that records the argv; asserts `--seats-pr <pr>` is invoked only when the file is empty/missing a seat (and not on the local path).
- Files touched: scripts/attribution_record.py, scripts/gaze_close.py, skills/merge/references/claims.md, skills/raid/SKILL.md, skills/hunt/SKILL.md, skills/gaze/SKILL.md, tests/test_attribution_record.py, tests/test_gaze_close.py. Registries: none (skills catalog unchanged unless a description changes; if so `make skills-catalog`).
- Dependencies: none blocking. Overlap with 1285/1287+ only if they edit gaze_close.py or raid SKILL.md Phase 5 (check the wave). Related 1243 closed context only.
- Exit mapping: 1 -> step 2 + gaze_close test; 2 -> step 1 + test 1; 3 -> steps 3-4 (grep that raid/hunt no longer list the fields); 4 -> `make` gate by the coder, quoting selected:/skipped:. Nothing needs a live credential; the gaze_close forge call is stubbed as in existing tests.

